An experiment in teaching an LLM to make calibrated trading decisions. I fine-tuned Qwen3-8B with LoRA on supervised examples, then trained it further with GRPO reinforcement learning against a market simulator I wrote in Rust, and ran the result as a paper trader on Modal.

The best run reached a profit factor of 1.27, a Brier score of 0.133 on its probability estimates and a 52% win rate in paper trading. Most of the work was in fighting reward hacking and policy collapse, and keeping a strict training journal.

Paper trading only; no real money.
